  "title": "Turkana Boy (KNM-WT 15000)",
  "summary": "A nearly complete early-human skeleton of a boy, catalogued KNM-WT 15000, was found at Nariokotome on the west side of Lake Turkana, Kenya, by Kamoya Kimeu in 1984. Dated to roughly 1.5 to 1.6 million years ago, it is classed as Homo erectus and records how an early human of that age was built.",
